    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "UNOVIS: The Suprematist Mirror, 1923",
      "links": [],
      "level": 4
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "In May 1923, the UNOVIS group, directed by Kazimir Malevich, showed 2 white monochromes in the exhibition Works of Petrograd Artists of All Movements at the Petrograd Art Academy. This presentation was accompanied by a manifesto entitled \"Suprematicheskoye zerkalo\" (\"The Suprematist Mirror\"), which goes far beyond Rodchenko's \"end of art\". Malevich embraces a radical, all-encompassing nihilism.",
      "links": []
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "\"The Suprematist Mirror\" was first published in Zhizn' Iskusstva # 20 (May 23, 1923), pp. 15-16. Excerpts were reprinted in Lef #3 (June-July 1923), pp. 182-183. To the right we reproduce the English translation by Xenia Giowacki-Prus & Arnold McMillin, from K.S. Malevich: Essays on Art, Vol.1. 1915-1928. Copenhagen: Borgen, 1971, pp. 224-225.",
      "links": []
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "The artists collective UNOVIS (the Champions of the New Art) was established in 1920 in Vitebsk. Its leader was Kazimir Malevich; the other members were Vera Ermolaeva,\nEl Lissitzky, Ilya Chashnik, Nikolai Suetin, Anna Leporskaya, Lev\nYudin, Evgenia Magaril, and Lazar Khidekel.",
      "links": [
        {
          "text": "UNOVIS (the Champions of the New Art",
          "href": "http://www.russianavantgard.com/unovis.html",
          "external": true
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Kazimir Malevich",
      "links": []
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "The Suprematist Mirror",
      "links": []
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Amongst all the changing phenomena the essence of nature is invariable.",
      "links": []
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "A. 1",
      "links": []
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "The World as\n\nhuman distinctions",
      "links": []
    },
    {
      "type": "figure",
      "src": "/images/nothing/monochrome/malevich-rodchenko/brackets-didot-left-narrow.gif",
      "alt": "",
      "caption": "",
      "width": null,
      "height": "220",
      "links": []
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "God\n\nThe Soul\n\nThe Spirit\n\nLife\n\nReligion\n\nTechnology\n\nArt\n\nScience\n\nThe Intellect\n\nWeltanschauung\n\nLabour\n\nMovement\n\nSpace\n\nTime",
      "links": []
    },
    {
      "type": "figure",
      "src": "/images/nothing/monochrome/malevich-rodchenko/brackets-didot-right-narrow.gif",
      "alt": "",
      "caption": "",
      "width": null,
      "height": "220",
      "links": []
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "= 0",
      "links": [],
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "1. Science and art have no boundaries because what is comprehended infinitely is innumerable and infinity and innumerability are equal to nothing.",
      "links": []
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "2. If the world's creations are God's paths and if \"His ways are inscrutable\", then both He and His path are equal to nothing.",
      "links": []
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "3. If the world is the creation of science, knowledge and labour, and if their creation is infinite then it is equal to nothing.",
      "links": []
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "4. If religion has comprehended God, it has comprehended nothing.",
      "links": []
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "5. If science has comprehended nature, it has comprehended nothing.",
      "links": []
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "6. If art has comprehended harmony, rhythm and beauty, it has comprehended nothing.",
      "links": []
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "7. If anyone has comprehended the absolute he has comprehended nothing.",
      "links": []
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "8. There is no existence either within or outside me; nothing can change anything, since nothing exists that could change itself or that could be changed.",
      "links": []
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "A. 2",
      "links": []
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "The essence of distinctions.\n\nThe world as non-objectivity.",
      "links": []
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Remko Scha, 2004/2010",
      "links": [
        {
          "text": "Remko Scha",
          "href": "http://iaaa.nl/rs/cv.html",
          "external": true
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
